Z||000000||GT GT 87||11-18-2001||08:28 PM|||| I am building a 3.2 with cam , headers , head work and ported intake and TB.  I was told to go to 3.4 injectors , what do they flow ??????  19 lbs.  ???????? there alot of ford 5.0 guys upgrading their cars and getting rid of their 19 lb. injectors.   Is that flow what I need ????????? do the ford ones have the correct impedence ???????   Please advive needed .  I'm almost done with my motor , I recently got a great looking clutch from Archie  !!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT GT 87||11-18-2001||11:42 PM||||Bump||||reg||1
Z||000002||SKIDMARK||11-18-2001||11:54 PM||||As far as I know, All GM mpi fuel systems run at 38 to 44 psi. I may be wrong though. The 3.4 injectors should work fine. A lot of guys have used the stock 3.4 injectors with their upgraded engines with decent results. As for Ford injectors, I'm reluctant to put anything with that name on my GM car so I never looked into it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||11-19-2001||12:12 AM||||There is a lot more to it than changing injectors...I don't care what anyone says.  If you don't change your computer it won't run right.<P>I've experienced this with my TEC-II.  Had to compensate with the IOT(injector offset time) to get the car to run...then I switched the flow rate on the injectors(in the program) and no longer needed any compensation.  Which happened to be like 19.?? for the 3400.<P>Unless you program your own chips, I say leave the injectors installed that the computer knows how to run.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT GT 87||11-19-2001||06:02 AM||||If I use 3.4 inj.s , what is their flow in lbs.  ??????  Has any one used the Fier store Tomco inj.s ?? What is their lb.- age ?????????????||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||11-19-2001||08:50 AM||||I have installed Ford Motorsports (Denso) 19 pound injectors in a friend's stock 86 GT. It was a little rich at first fire up, but after driving, the BLM dropped to 120 (the ECM compensated for the extra fuel). It runs better than it has since he has owned the car because 4 of the 6 old injectors were leaking badly. I will get the car soon and burn a chip to compensate for the extra fuel if needed.||||reg||1
